     eedd is a line-oriented text editor.  It reads commands from
     the standard input, normally one command per line, and edits
     a copy of the text held in memory; no change reaches a file
     until a ww command writes it out.  If the optional _f_i_l_e argu-
     ment is given, eedd reads it in as though by the ee command
     below.

     eedd keeps a _c_u_r_r_e_n_t _l_i_n_e , initially the last line read in
     and thereafter the line most recently addressed or affected
     by a command, and a _c_u_r_r_e_n_t _f_i_l_e _n_a_m_e , last set by an ee , EE
     , or ff command.

