OOppttiioonnss
     The _o_p_t_i_o_n_s recognized by the oo command, on the command line
     with a leading +, and in the environment variable EEDD are:

     cc   Print character counts after ee, rr, and ww commands (set
         by default).

     mm   Allow more than one command on a line.

     oo   Print line counts, rather than character counts, after
         ee, rr, and ww commands.

     pp   Prompt with * before reading each command.

     ss   Make lower-case letters in a pattern match either case
         in the text.

     vv   Print a fuller message after an error, rather than just
         ?.

     Preceding a letter with - resets the option instead of set-
     ting it.

